\chapter{The Application and Its Scenes}\label{ch:app}

A SwiftUI application is a value of a type that conforms to [[App]] and describes its
\emph{scenes}: windows, and on visionOS immersive spaces. This chapter presents the application
type, the model it owns, and two small companions.

\section{The application}

[[ViewerApp]] imports CloudXRKit unconditionally and Foveated Streaming only when the
[[FOVEATED_STREAMING]] condition is set. That condition, defined in [[Config.xcconfig]]
(Section~\ref{sec:condition}), is on for device builds and off for the simulator, which has no
Foveated Streaming framework. The three strings name the scenes so that code elsewhere can open
and dismiss them.

<<CloudXRViewer/Common/ViewerApp.swift>>=
<<NVIDIA license header>>

import CloudXRKit
import SwiftUI
import simd

#if os(visionOS)
// For measuring render camera positions.
import CompositorServices
#endif
#if FOVEATED_STREAMING && os(visionOS)
import FoveatedStreaming
#endif

let launchTitle = "launch"
let contentTitle = "content"
let immersiveTitle = "immersive"

@
The application owns the [[AppModel]] as state, so the model lives as long as the
application does. On visionOS it also keeps the actions that open and dismiss immersive spaces and
a user setting that decides whether the launch window stays visible while streaming.

<<CloudXRViewer/Common/ViewerApp.swift>>=
@main
struct ViewerApp: App {
    @UIApplicationDelegateAdaptor(AppDelegate.self) var appDelegate
    @Environment(\.scenePhase) var scenePhase
    @Environment(\.openWindow) private var openWindow
    @Environment(\.dismissWindow) private var dismissWindow

    @State private var appModel = AppModel()
    @State var showDisconnectionErrorAlert = false

#if os(visionOS)
    @Environment(\.dismissImmersiveSpace) private var dismissImmersiveSpace
    @Environment(\.openImmersiveSpace) private var openImmersiveSpace
    @AppStorage("persistLaunchWindow") static var persistLaunchWindow = true
#endif


    // Window sizes
    static let launchSize = CGSize(width: 680, height: 900)

@
[[CloudXRKit.registerSystems()]] registers CloudXRKit's RealityKit systems, which draw
the classic stream. Foveated Streaming needs no such registration: the system draws its stream.

<<CloudXRViewer/Common/ViewerApp.swift>>=
    init() {
        CloudXRKit.registerSystems()

#if os(visionOS)
        // For tests.
        TestHelper.appModel = appModel


        appDelegate.session = appModel.session
#endif
    }

@
\subsection{Scenes on visionOS}

The launch window shows the configuration form. Two observers matter here. The pause sheet
modifier, compiled only with Foveated Streaming, lets the system show its own sheet when a
foveated session is paused (Section~\ref{sec:pausesheet}). The [[onChange]] observer forwards every
connection change to the window manager (Chapter~\ref{ch:visionos}). It observes
[[connectionState]], the pair of backend and status, and ignores a change whose backend differs
from the previous one: switching the backend picker changes [[appModel.status]] too, from the
status of one session to that of the other, and without the guard a switch back to a backend
whose last session had failed would replay its disconnection as if it had just happened.

<<CloudXRViewer/Common/ViewerApp.swift>>=
#if os(visionOS)
    var body: some Scene {
        WindowGroup(id: launchTitle) {
            LaunchView(application: $appModel.application)
                .environment(appModel)
                .frame(
                    // Fixed-size window
                    minWidth: Self.launchSize.width,
                    maxWidth: Self.launchSize.width,
                    minHeight: Self.launchSize.height,
                    maxHeight: Self.launchSize.height
                )
                .alert(isPresented: $showDisconnectionErrorAlert) {
                    makeDisconnectionAlert()
                }
#if FOVEATED_STREAMING
                .foveatedStreamingPauseSheet(session: foveatedPauseSheetSession)
#endif
                .onAppear {
                    appModel.windowStateManager.configure(
                        appModel: appModel,
                        openImmersiveSpace: openImmersiveSpace,
                        dismissImmersiveSpace: dismissImmersiveSpace,
                        openWindow: openWindow,
                        dismissWindow: dismissWindow
                    )
                    appModel.windowStateManager.windowOnAppear(windowId: launchTitle)
                }
                .onDisappear {
                    appModel.windowStateManager.windowOnDisappear(windowId: launchTitle)
                }
                .onChange(of: appModel.connectionState) { oldState, newState in
                    guard oldState.backend == newState.backend else { return }
                    Task {
                        await appModel.windowStateManager.onConnectionStateChanged(oldState: oldState.status, newState: newState.status)
                    }
                }
        }
        .defaultSize(Self.launchSize)
        .windowResizability(.contentSize)
        .defaultWindowPlacement { content, context in
            if let contentWindow = context.windows.first(
                where: { $0.id == contentTitle }) {
                WindowPlacement(.leading(contentWindow))
            } else {
                WindowPlacement()
            }
        }

